    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n52514" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κᾰλαμ-ίτης</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῑ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καλάμινος</span>
			, <i>reed-like</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στύραξ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alex.Trall.
					5.4
				</span></i>
			, al., <i><span class="en">
				Aët.
				1.133
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ κ. ἥρως</span>, perh. the hero <i>of
				the probe</i> or, <i>of the splints</i>, nickname of
			Aristomachus, a surgeon who had a statue at Athens, called <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ ἥρως ὁ ἰατρός</span>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				18.129
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				19.249
			</span></i>.</div>
